{
    "controller_name": "Cummins PCC1302",
    "information": "Cummins PowerCommand PCC1302 (PowerCommand 1.x family) over Modbus RTU on the controller's RS485 port (PCC1302 TB15-3 A+, TB15-4 B-, TB15-1 common). Register map from Cummins document A029X159, section 'PCC 1301/PowerCommand 1.x/PS0500 Modbus Register Map'. Typical comms 9600 baud, even parity (genmon.conf: serial_parity = even), slave address 1. READ-ONLY profile: no buttons, no settime. The rated voltage, frequency and phase are read from the controller (43000-43002); until they are read genmon's settings are used. The controller has no rated kW, RPM or battery voltage registers: set Nominal RPM, Maximum kW Output and Nominal Battery Voltage in genmon's settings. Tested on a 36 kW natural gas C36N6 genset (controller type code 71).",
    "register_format_info": "Addresses are 0-based Modbus PDU addresses in hex: Cummins 4xxxx = (xxxx - 1), e.g. 40010 -> 0009. The controller accepts reads of 1-16 contiguous registers and rejects a block containing an unimplemented address, so each register is declared on its own.",
    "rated_max_output_power_kw": "Unknown",
